<description>&lt;p&gt;Heavy fighting between government forces and opposition resulted in 23 deaths in recent clashes. South Sudan released the bodies of two Ugandan truck drivers killed in an ambush, a commissioner in Mayom County and his family were assassinated, and a soldier and a civilian were killed in a Kapoeta North attack. Governors in Jonglei and Aweil East called for peace and justice after violence in Uror and two killings, local peace talks began in Tonj East to end communal violence, churches report disruption of worship due to deadly communal clashes, and the ICRC reported ongoing sexual violence. Two battle-related deaths were recorded in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Hindu&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMid0FVX3lxTE5ScDR4ODFLdHBhU3ZPVFdPRHZSOGZ4Nmo1WnhXQ0lXVUxGZGFTLUYwS0JMTmtpQ1diMGw1b2ctRFRMeTVKcC1NbjhKZ3lCY0t2QUNnYVRlVnY1Uy1PcXhrZjBOdVdwdnJXdFU0aDZvU09xbkRrazdN?oc=5&quot;&gt;Times of Suriname&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiaEFVX3lxTE43ZGR3Wno1WHpjU2ExOFpXTHlRZVZpU2Y1eHhEdGlNSkhpQm9GYXFRUjJ0V1lkWThHUjFpSks0MFhHMFNQM3FUU3Y4OTNVOERuUWJEbnhDNlNoelhwS1BBVklGNC1NVElH?oc=5&quot;&gt;Uganda Radionetwork&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMirwFBVV95cUxQdjhZWXJxam1YWm00dVluZzB4TmlYbzNCd193NG1pamphSlFseDEyRjFDM1FIMzJjN3BVLUFvUUxJRDFld3hWVmxDVkFkRG1mek85TzhWeDF1dkxvNm9TY2U0QjdqRk5jNVQtM25FVXFaOGZISWJyTkRiZDlBRlltYlBIQTZHY1dTQkcwaXFLWGstV0ZaSFZ2NWtWZ2tBb1N3aUR2ZmNTODRQSENXaTFZ?oc=5&quot;&gt;www.christiandaily.com&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Eye Radio&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiZEFVX3lxTE9XYXRtdUVzUzllcEI2TDVVUmd4clM0SEEtNlBtOXNKSWhUWUdWUk9tUVlSQmNralRkR2ZoSW1GeW9rV0VTTGJvYkcxZE5LQWpQN2ZDOG43ZE